  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Given that the differential equation \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4y=5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\n$$\n\nhas the complementary solution ${y}_{c}(x)=A{e}^{4x}$, find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ to this equation.\n\n${y}_{p}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To find the general solution of an inhomogeneous first-order linear equation with constant coefficients on the left-hand side, we must find the sum of the complementary and particular solutions.\n\nThe right-hand side of the inhomogeneous equation is $5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x.$ So, we assume the particular solution to be \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x.\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first derivative of ${y}_{p}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x}=-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x.\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute ${y}_{p}$ and ${y}_{p}^{\u2032}$ into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x)-4(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)=5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x.\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n(\\beta -4\\alpha )\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x+(-\\alpha -4\\beta )\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x=5\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\beta -4\\alpha =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x) \\\\ -\\alpha -4\\beta =5\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{5}{17},$ $\\beta =-\\frac{20}{17}.$\n\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{5}{17}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(x)-\\frac{20}{17}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(x).\n$$",
